Package: fLSL
Type: Package
Title: Functional Spatial-Index Logit Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Muge", "Mutis", email = "muge.mutis@yildiz.edu.tr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimation and inference for a functional spatial-index logit model, in which a scalar on-function index is propagated across spatial units by a spatial autoregressive multiplier and linked to the success probability of a binary response through a logistic function. The curves are represented by functional principal component analysis. The package provides the one-step functional linearized spatial logit (FLSL) estimator and its inversion-free Wald test of no spatial propagation, the iterated projected generalized method of moments estimator computed by a safeguarded Gauss-Newton iteration (IFLSL-LS), spatial heteroskedasticity and autocorrelation consistent (HAC) inference, average direct, indirect and total functional effect curves with pointwise bands, Bernoulli quasi-maximum likelihood and nonlinear least squares benchmarks, diagnostics and the simulation designs of the accompanying paper.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: fda, graphics, Matrix, methods, stats, utils
Suggests: dbscan, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/MugeMutis/fLSL
